In video-less SDL builds (SDL_VIDEO=OFF, as vendored here) there is no helper
window, and DirectInput rejects an exclusive cooperative level with a NULL
window, so every DirectInput-mode controller enumerated but failed to open.
Open in non-exclusive background mode instead when there is no helper window.

Upstreamed as https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/pull/16207 - drop this patch
once the vendored SDL includes the fix.

diff --git a/src/joystick/windows/SDL_dinputjoystick.c b/src/joystick/windows/SDL_dinputjoystick.c
index 73c26051..e99dba07 100644
--- a/src/joystick/windows/SDL_dinputjoystick.c
+++ b/src/joystick/windows/SDL_dinputjoystick.c
@@ -764,10 +764,13 @@ int SDL_DINPUT_JoystickOpen(SDL_Joystick *joystick, JoyStick_DeviceData *joystic
     }
 
     /* Acquire shared access. Exclusive access is required for forces,
-     * though. */
+     * though. In a build without the Windows video driver there is no helper
+     * window, and exclusive mode requires a valid window handle; DirectInput
+     * only allows a NULL window with non-exclusive background mode, so use
+     * that (giving up force feedback) rather than failing the open. */
     result =
         IDirectInputDevice8_SetCooperativeLevel(joystick->hwdata->InputDevice, SDL_HelperWindow,
-                                                DISCL_EXCLUSIVE |
+                                                (SDL_HelperWindow ? DISCL_EXCLUSIVE : DISCL_NONEXCLUSIVE) |
                                                     DISCL_BACKGROUND);
     if (FAILED(result)) {
         return SetDIerror("IDirectInputDevice8::SetCooperativeLevel", result);
